# Example 30: virtual-cell calibration -> prediction workflow (S9)
# The whole-cell-modeling validation loop in miniature, mirroring the
# "calibrate then predict" protocol of the Virtual Cell Challenge 2025:
# a VirtualCell (central dogma + GRN + FBA metabolism + cell-cycle energy
# budget, Karr et al. 2012) is *calibrated* on one growth condition and
# then *predicts* an independent condition from fitted parameters alone.
#
# The benchmark in helixlang.apps.virtual_cell_bench hides a true
# biomass-to-ATP conversion constant (5.0e6) behind a synthetic trajectory
# (GLC 10 mM, 20 min).  A calibration pass searches + refines that constant
# from the observed energy alone, then the fitted model predicts a harder
# condition (GLC 20 mM, 60 min) and must land on the ground-truth energy:
#
#   fit        -> biomass_to_atp 5.000e6 (truth 5.000e6, rel err 0.0%)
#   prediction -> energy 284,982,601 ATP (alive=True, proteins=3), alive
#                 and protein counts match the ground-truth model exactly
#   benchmark  -> passed (calibrated=True, predicted=True)
#
#gene name=virtual_cell
ATG GCT GGT GTA TAA
#end
#
#config ticks=100 output=stdout
